From fe4381496c9e343f30036d1af7ffffab6c681c91 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: fozzfut <vanolia13@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 01:07:41 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] PartDesign: Chamfer measures Size and Angle on one
 consistent face per edge

Two distances / Distance and Angle handed BRepFilletAPI_MakeChamfer the
first adjacent face of each edge in TopExp ancestor order (FlipDirection:
the last). OCCT measures Dis1 / Dis on that face and the angle from it,
exactly (checked against the analytic normal-section triangle, 0 difference
between OCCT 7.8.1 and 8.0.1), so the topology order alone decided which
face got Size: the side face of a pad's top edge, the cylinder of a boss
rim, and on an imported part's face rim three edges on the face and one on
the wall. 51 of 94 ground-truth rows were wrong.

New property ReferenceMode:
- Consistent (new chamfers): a face picked in Base, else the face shared
  by the most chamfered edges (the face the chain runs around), else a
  planar face, else the larger face; FlipDirection takes the other face of
  every edge. Size / Size2 / Angle go to Add(d1, d2, E, F) / AddDA(d, a, E, F).
- Legacy: the old topology-order choice, same geometry as before. Restore()
  sets Legacy first, so documents saved without the property keep their
  geometry.

New output property ReferenceFaces ("EdgeN:FaceM", not saved) records the
face each edge was measured on. The task panel puts the Size gizmo on that
face and re-places the gizmos after a type change, so the gizmo, the
result and the record agree.

Distance and Angle that can never reach the other face (angle plus the
dihedral angle >= 180 deg) now fails with a message naming the edge, the
faces and both angles instead of "BRep_API: command not done".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
